How can I calculate the probability of "The Celtics win the game" in the next game, given that it had an 80% success rate in the last 10 games? Can you provide me with a C# function that takes in the number of successes and total trials as input and returns the probability of success?
[C# code] 
public double CalculateProbability(int numSuccesses, int totalTrials)
{
    double successRate = 0.8;
    double probability = 0.0;

    // Calculate the probability of success
    for (int i = numSuccesses; i <= totalTrials; i++)
    {
        double combination = Factorial(totalTrials) / (Factorial(i) * Factorial(totalTrials - i));
        probability += combination * Math.Pow(successRate, i) * Math.Pow(1 - successRate, totalTrials - i);
    }

    return probability;
}
private double Factorial(int num)
{
    double result = 1.0;

    for (int i = 1; i <= num; i++)
    {
        result *= i;
    }

    return result;
}
This function takes in the number of successes and total trials as input and returns the probability of success based on the given success rate. You can call this function by passing the number of successes and total trials as arguments.

