\subsection{Analysis}
Each of the individuals listed in Table \ref{table:1} has made significant contributions to the field of art. Leonardo da Vinci is known for his mastery of multiple disciplines, including painting, sculpture, and engineering. His use of sfumato in his paintings is still admired today. Pablo Picasso co-founded the Cubist movement, which revolutionized modern art. Vincent van Gogh's use of bold colors and thick brushstrokes influenced many artists who came after him. Michelangelo's mastery of the human form and his use of chiaroscuro are still admired today. Claude Monet co-founded the Impressionist movement, which emphasized the use of light and color in art. Rembrandt van Rijn's ability to capture the human soul in his paintings is still admired today. Salvador Dalí's surrealistic paintings continue to fascinate viewers. Johannes Vermeer's use of light and color in his paintings is still admired today. Jackson Pollock's unique style of drip painting has influenced many artists who came after him. Andy Warhol's use of pop culture imagery in his art has had a lasting impact on the art world.
However, each of these individuals has also faced criticism and controversy. For example, some have criticized Michelangelo's portrayal of women in his art as being overly sexualized. Similarly, some have criticized Salvador Dalí's use of bizarre and sometimes disturbing imagery in his art. Additionally, some have criticized Andy Warhol for commercializing art and turning it into a commodity.
